      "content": "To detect these patterns, you'll need specialized equipment like a high-sensitivity spectrum analyzer or a precision acoustic monitor capable of capturing sub-audible frequencies. Since the hum is linked to system changes, correlating your anxiety log with precise times of lighting shifts is the key to triangulation. You could potentially use a data logging system to record the system operational status simultaneously with capturing the ambient sound spectrum during those transitions.",
      "source": "target",
